WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.102
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.104
to try each other's Burger Kings.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.472
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.309
So, obviously you can get a Whopper meal

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.810
at a UK and a US Burger King.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.212
But we did want to get
them in both countries

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.947
and compare the two to
see the differences.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.749
This here of course is
a standard Whopper meal.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.350
I believe it was the regular size.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.253
And this would be a small in the US.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.521
Just a quick visual check,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.823
I mean, the Whopper itself looks identical

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.725
to the Whopper that I'm
used to seeing in the UK.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.027
Really, really no changes there.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.895
The toppings seem to be the same.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.998
You get the mayo, the pickles,
the lettuce, the tomato,

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.067
onions, and of course
the beef on a sesame bun.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.935
So that's, yeah, exactly what I'm used to.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.239
Let's take a look at a UK Whopper.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.910
Looks exactly the same, so that's good.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.614
Same size. Yeah, it's a big one, right?

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.349
Same stuff on the inside.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.717
Oh, and I got a regular one.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.453
I didn't even get it with
cheese, which is rare for me.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.656
That tastes pretty similar
to what I'm used to.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.492
The beef is pretty
similar, if not identical.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.528
You still get that flame-grilled thing

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.596
that Burger King is kind of known for.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.633
American mayo so far has
just been very creamy,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.234
but pretty much everything
else is the same.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.003
Overall, very similar to the
Whopper that I'm used to.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:15.008
Exactly the same, which is
good. But the fries, however,

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.476
your fries are a bit different, I think.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.579
Honestly, the fries, this
is a large Whopper meal.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.415
I was kind of expecting
bigger for the US, you know?

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.784
There's a good portion of
fries, don't get me wrong.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.920
But I feel like in the US,
if you order a large fries,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.721
I was expecting, like, a lot of fries.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.757
They look pretty similar to
the fries that I'm used to.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.025
They're fairly thick-cut,

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:34.094
thicker-cut than, like, a McDonald's, so.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.431
These are pretty good
fries, I have to say.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.567
I feel like when I go to
a Burger King in the UK,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.001
I'm not really there for the fries.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.671
The fries are just very much
a sort of add-on to the meal.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.439
These are good. These taste way better

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.841
than the fries that I'm
used to from Burger King.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.075
I don't know what
they've done differently.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.177
They're quite aggressively salted,

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.545
which I personally really like.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.847
But they're just well cooked.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.316
There's a little bit of
crisp on the outside.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.551
Still quite nice and fluffy on the inside.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.221
The US Burger King has —
the fries are weird.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:05.091
There's some sort of batter to them.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.727
I can't describe it. They
changed it years ago,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.396
and they're a more distinct flavor.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.132
I don't dislike them,
but they're not that great.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.400
These regular fries, I think I prefer

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.137
the UK Burger King fries
over the US ones, definitely.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.671
And of course, the fountain Coke.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.473
I hope that the camera can capture

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.742
the scale of just how large this drink is.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.511
I have a big head.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.516
Yeah, I mean, it's
fountain Coke. It's fine.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.251
Yeah, this regular drink is so tiny.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.552
I've just been informed that a whopper

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:35.288
can be considered an insult
in the UK. What does it mean?

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.893
That's funny.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:42.428
Have you been called a whopper before?

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.463
Someone called you a whopper?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.303
I think generally
speaking, fairly familiar.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.539
Pretty much what I'm used
to in terms of the burger.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.506
I've enjoyed these fries

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.341
more than I enjoy the British fries.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.377
And the Coke is too big.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.212
Dial that back a little
bit, guys. Calm down.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.284
Here's everything you
can get at a BK in the US

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.685
that you can't find in the UK.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.655
Here are all the UK Burger King menu items

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.590
I cannot get in the US.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.692
Let's take a look at
the US beef exclusives.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.562
We'll start with this, the Whopper Jr.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.597
Look at this thing. It's tiny!

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.632
I mean, yeah, I think it's
just a scaled-down version

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.568
of the Whopper. It's got all
the same toppings on there.

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.936
Now we're going from one end of the scale

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:23.870
straight to the other.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.240
We're going from the junior
Whopper to the triple Whopper.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.642
As the name suggests, it is a Whopper,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.412
but instead of the one
patty, you get three.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.981
I mean, I don't necessarily object

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.116
to the existence of a triple Whopper.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.619
I will say I've got some
notes on the assembly,

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.588
because there's no layering going on.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.189
Obviously a Whopper doesn't have cheese.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.491
This is literally just the toppings

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.861
and then just three meat
patties back to back.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.463
So I feel like when you bite into this,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:54.167
you're just going to get a
big mouthful of just beef.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.768
I mean, I will try it for science.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.770
I'll take a little bite of the triple.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.208
Yeah, that's kind of confirmed my fears.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.509
I'm also covered in mayo.

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.178
Next up, we're off to Texas,

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.180
because this is a Texas Whopper.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.881
In case you're wondering
what made this Texan,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.683
it seems like they've just added

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:13.886
some jalapeños,
bacon, cheese,

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:14.454
and mustard

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:15.788
to a standard
Whopper.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.657
I don't really know
enough about Texas culture

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.525
to know if that makes
something Texan or not.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.995
I would've expected
maybe some barbecue sauce

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.196
if you call something Texan,

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.498
but they seem to have not
done that. So, we'll see.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.636
I'm a big mustard fan,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.471
so I like the inclusion
of mustard on this.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.940
Yeah, that's not bad. I don't
know if I would order that

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.108
just over a standard Whopper,

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.809
but I think it's better
than a triple Whopper.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.711
This is the BK double melt,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:42.682
with a signature cheesy sauce
instead of a slab of cheese.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.885
They just drizzled the, excuse
me, melted liquid cheese.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.187
The melted cheese is kind
of a nice texture to it.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.757
A slice of cheese would
just as easily suffice.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:54.927
Bacon double cheeseburger XL, Charlie.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.930
Two patties, cheese in the
middle, cheese in between them.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.199
Very smart, guys. See?
It makes a difference.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.167
It's bigger than — in America,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.703
we have the regular bacon
double cheeseburger.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.005
This one is a little bit bigger.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.741
Well, it's extra bigger. So there you go.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.678
Yeah, I like this.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.647
And I would probably get this
if I went to Burger King.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.616
I think this would do
really well in America.

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:18.818
Come on, two big beef patties,

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.688
dripping with cheese
and bacon. And it's big.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:24.390
It's like, its selling
point is that it's big.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.192
Dude, this would clean up in the US.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:28.027
If this is in the US,
we gotta get US bacon.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.897
Look at this. Come on, guys, look at this.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:33.232
How, like, not pink this is.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.234
This is like, oh, this bacon's bad.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.602
Then we have two more burger exclusives,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:40.273
which are the kings.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:43.176
First up, we have the
Single Quarter Pound King.

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.511
This is a single quarter-pound patty

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:49.582
with some onions, pickles,
cheese, mustard, and ketchup.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.983
This looks pretty good
to me. This looks like

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.386
a very classic hamburger,
which I'm kind of here for.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:54.921
I will say, in general,
what I'm really enjoying

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.622
about all of these burgers is the pickles.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.459
I feel like America does
pickles way better than we do.

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.993
I thought that was going
to be better than it was.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.595
I don't know why. I don't
know what's wrong with it.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.163
There's quite a lot of onion in it.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.232
Just a lot of raw white onion.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.066
And then the next one

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.601
I think we might have
had recently on the menu,

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.103
or it might still be
on the menu in the UK,

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:12.004
but is a bacon king.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.673
Either way, I thought this
would be a good opportunity

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.341
to talk about fast-food bacon.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.542
This is a double burger,

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.378
some cheese in the middle and on top,

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:23.349
along with a few rashers of
bacon, some ketchup, and mayo.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:27.253
Let me just prize a bit of
this bacon off this burger

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.888
so we can get a closer look.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:32.892
So, this is the famous
American fast-food bacon.

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.561
So, I feel like the US and
the UK do fast-food bacon,

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:38.097
and I guess bacon in
general, pretty differently.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:41.234
This in the UK would be
called a streaky bacon rasher,

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.035
which is where you get
the kind of thin strips,

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:45.405
as opposed to back bacon,
where you have a medallion

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.939
and then some strip coming off it.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.841
Generally speaking, in
the UK, fast-food bacon

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:52.378
tends to be quite a pallid
pink, fairly unappealing color,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.746
and can be quite floppy as well.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:55.515
They don't tend to cook it
basically for long enough.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:58.017
I will say this bacon has
a lot more color on it

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.753
than I would expect to see
from British fast-food bacon.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.990
That's pretty good. I think
that's probably better than

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.160
the bacon that I'm used to
from a British fast-food chain.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.128
So far, all the bacon I've
had, including this one,

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:10.563
it just tends to have a better texture.

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:11.798
There's a bit more chew to it.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:14.000
It's just been cooked a
little bit longer, I think.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.402
Also, it lends itself to
giving it a much nicer color.

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.738
And you definitely get more
of a smoky flavor from it

00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:20.206
that you would expect from good bacon,

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:23.009
which I don't think you tend
to get from UK fast-food bacon.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:27.814
Yeah, the gourmet kings.
Let's go! Ooh! Fancy.

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:30.516
First one, farmhouse,
straight from the farm.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:33.352
You got your rocket, aka arugula.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:36.489
You got your ... pickled red onions?

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:38.324
And, like, a smoky cheddar cheese, right?

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:39.692
This is actually,

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.060
this is pretty impressive
looking, I gotta say.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:44.931
Ooh, brioche bun.

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:46.032
Now here we go.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.769
The arugula, or rocket, kind of ruins it.

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:54.140
I like it, but it's such a strong flavor,

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.544
it just really tastes like
arugula, rocket, whatever.

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:00.112
So having a bite without
it is a lot better.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:03.082
So, unfortunately I think
the arugula's a little much.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:06.285
This one also has arugula on it, so uh-oh.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.220
Let's get a look in there, man.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:11.424
They got the barbecue
sauce, crispy onions, right?

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:13.759
And the same cheddar, same fun cheddar.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.428
The arugula's kind of still
a little overpowering,

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:17.330
but with the fun stuff, and
this cheese that's on here

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.499
is really good, the smoked cheddar.

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.567
This one's good. I would
get this. I like this.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.202
So steakhouse over farmhouse.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:24.403
Then we have a couple of very adorable

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:26.138
tiny burgers down at the end.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.341
This one is the Rodeo burger.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.776
So we're going back to
the South for this one.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.378
To make this Rodeo, they've added

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.514
barbecue sauce and some onion rings.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.549
See, the only reason I
can think of onion rings

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:37.783
counting as Rodeo is that

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.886
maybe it looks a little bit like a lasso.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:42.421
Lasso.

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:43.422
No.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:45.491
And then finally we just
have a double cheeseburger.

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:48.127
You guys got the Memphis barbecue burgers,

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:50.696
single and double. Go side by side.

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.198
You know, we, in the US, we got something

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:55.268
called the Rodeo burger. I
don't think you have that here.

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:57.169
Where it's onion rings and barbecue sauce,

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.538
and it's surprisingly good.

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:02.008
But it's, like, the smallest
thing. It's, like, that big.

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:06.579
But this is a good idea.
This is that, but adult size.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:07.980
Yeah!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.348
I gotta get a bite, but I gotta make sure

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.784
I get an onion ring in it, so.

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.786
This works really well together.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:15.221
This all works. The creamy mayo,

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.856
the mayo and the barbecue sauce

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:19.892
and the onion rings, and the bacon?

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.561
Yeah, dude, this is good!

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:23.629
Another thing that would
do so well in the US.

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:25.031
I don't know why we don't have this

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:26.666
in the States, as you say.

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:27.967
I will say, they'd have to rename it.

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:30.369
It'd have to be, like, the Rodeo
burger deluxe or something.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.138
I don't know what about this is Memphis.

00:09:32.138 --> 00:09:34.407
I mean, the barbecue
sauce, it's a sweet sauce.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:37.843
I don't know what makes it
"Memphis-y" specifically.

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:41.280
And I'm still not clear on
why onion rings equals Rodeo.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.749
Then we're on to some chicken,
fish, and side options.

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.685
We'll start with these ones,
which are chicken fries.

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:46.752
Now, I'm pretty sure we can get these

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.721
or have had these in the UK before.

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:50.189
However, when we were recording this,

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:51.691
it seems as if the only ones available

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:53.960
are the Doritos chili heatwave version,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.495
whereas these are the
old-fashioned classic ones.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.064
These things are great. I love these.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:00.967
I don't want to know how
they form the chicken

00:10:00.967 --> 00:10:02.568
into long strips like this.

00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:05.037
If British people are
familiar with Fridge Raiders,

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:07.540
the snacks, kind of like a bigger,

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.108
hotter version of those. It's great.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:10.977
Next up we have a chicken sandwich option,

00:10:10.977 --> 00:10:12.812
which is the chicken Jr.

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:14.480
As Joe just pointed out,
they love calling things

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.683
"Jr." at Burger King in the US.

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:20.620
Personally, I think they
should be called the prince.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:24.156
You know? You have the
Burger King as the main one.

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:25.658
The little one should be a prince, surely.

00:10:25.658 --> 00:10:27.560
Like a chicken duke,

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.430
or archbishop of beef.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.165
It just looks like a very
simple chicken burger.

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:36.369
That's pretty good.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:39.038
The mayo's quite creamy and quite sweet.

00:10:39.038 --> 00:10:41.207
Chicken royale. Looks
just like the regular

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:44.477
original chicken sandwich we got at BK.

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:47.013
Longer, though.

00:10:47.013 --> 00:10:48.447
Ah.

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:51.984
Oh, wait, but this one
has cheese and bacon.

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:55.855
Hm. Yeah, this looks kind of upsetting.

00:10:57.523 --> 00:10:58.691
Kind of a bummer.

00:10:58.691 --> 00:11:01.327
OK, crispy chicken Memphis style.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:02.895
I do like the Memphis style.

00:11:02.895 --> 00:11:06.098
Onion rings and bacon
and chicken with cheese?

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:08.100
That's a new combination right?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.970
Yeah. Yeah to this. Yeah!

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.305
I think because it's fried chicken,

00:11:13.305 --> 00:11:16.642
it adds even more flavor to it,

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:18.411
with the bacon, cheese, and onion rings.

00:11:18.411 --> 00:11:22.381
It's a bit much, but it actually
works pretty well together.

00:11:22.381 --> 00:11:27.219
I think we gotta Memphis up
some of our BK in the US.

00:11:27.219 --> 00:11:29.588
Or just call it Rodeo-style it up.

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:32.224
Then we have a fish option, the big fish.

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:35.594
It's fairly reminiscent of a
Filet-O-Fish from McDonald's,

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:37.396
in that it's got that kind of shiny bun.

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:39.832
I do like a good fish sandwich.

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:42.768
Yeah, that's really not bad.

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:45.838
The fish is, like, fine.
It doesn't taste of a ton.

00:11:45.838 --> 00:11:47.406
An acceptable attempt at a fish sandwich.

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.542
Probably not quite as
good as a Filet-O-Fish.

00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:51.677
Then we have a side option
we can't find in the UK.

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:53.746
It's mozzarella sticks.

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:55.648
I feel like, yeah, we have now hit a point

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:58.050
where pretty much everywhere
does its own mozzarella stick.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.119
What I will say is it
comes with a little thing

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:02.588
of marinara sauce, which
I think is the only

00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:07.059
exclusive sauce at a US Burger King.

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:10.296
So we can do a very,
very short sauce talk.

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:11.163
Sauce talk.

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.398
The sauce is pretty strong, actually.

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:15.167
That's a concentrated tomato flavor.

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:17.336
It's almost like eating a tomato puree

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:19.004
rather than a marinara sauce.

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:20.439
Acceptable mozzarella sticks.

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.108
I probably wouldn't be
rushing toward those again.

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:23.042
Plant-based Whopper.

00:12:23.042 --> 00:12:25.044
I'm pretty sure I did
this in the US, right?

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:28.981
But your guys' plant-based
meat is different than ours.

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:32.985
We have the Impossible meat in the US.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:37.356
So, our Impossible
Whopper, Impossible meat

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:41.427
has a chemical that is under review.

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:43.896
You guys have a different
plant-based meat than we do.

00:12:43.896 --> 00:12:45.598
So let's see what it tastes like.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:49.034
It's not ... bad.

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:54.073
It's not flame-grilled-flavored enough,

00:12:54.073 --> 00:12:54.940
you know what I mean?

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.942
Like, the Whopper, the
meat, you just taste

00:12:56.942 --> 00:12:59.945
that grill smokiness, charcoaliness,

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:01.680
whatever you want to call it.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.282
And this, it looks like
they cooked it the same way,

00:13:03.282 --> 00:13:05.518
but I'm not getting that same
flavor from this meat at all.

00:13:05.518 --> 00:13:06.886
So it still tastes like meat,

00:13:06.886 --> 00:13:07.787
but it doesn't taste like a Whopper.

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:10.289
It doesn't have that
smoky flavor to it. So.

00:13:10.289 --> 00:13:12.892
And I don't think that has
anything to do with the meat.

00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:15.961
I think you guys have got
to flame grill it more

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:18.063
or add the same flame-grill
chemicals onto this

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:19.231
as you do the regular meat.

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:23.002
This is noticeably different
than the UK Whopper.

00:13:23.002 --> 00:13:24.403
Vegan chicken.

00:13:25.337 --> 00:13:27.239
Ew.

00:13:27.239 --> 00:13:30.543
This looks exactly like the
original chicken sandwich, so.

00:13:32.545 --> 00:13:34.613
There's something weird in here.

00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:36.248
There's something weird to that flavor.

00:13:36.248 --> 00:13:37.650
I'm just going to take a little —

00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:42.588
Oh, this is not a good sign.

00:13:42.588 --> 00:13:44.390
This meat is not easy to pull apart.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.192
Ah! Ugh.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.195
Nah, it just tastes weird.

00:13:49.195 --> 00:13:50.896
It doesn't taste like chicken.

00:13:50.896 --> 00:13:53.299
It tastes like it's
flavored like the chicken.

00:13:53.299 --> 00:13:56.168
But the consistency of
it is just different.

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:57.903
I wouldn't say it was bad.

00:13:57.903 --> 00:14:00.806
It just tastes like it's not chicken.

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:02.374
These came and went in the US so fast,

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:04.109
I didn't get a chance to try them.

00:14:04.109 --> 00:14:05.845
But now I finally do.

00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:07.279
Looks like a nugget.

00:14:09.348 --> 00:14:11.517
Yeah, it just tastes like
a fake something or other.

00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:14.820
Maybe the batter on this seems
thicker than regular nuggets,

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.388
so I'm getting almost all batter flavor,

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:17.623
which I guess isn't that big of a deal.

00:14:17.623 --> 00:14:18.924
This doesn't taste like chicken.

00:14:18.924 --> 00:14:21.193
Again, it's, like, blank.

00:14:21.193 --> 00:14:22.895
It doesn't have much flavor to it.

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:24.897
Yeah, I mean, I think
you guys gotta step up

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:28.267
your chemical game, because our
fake meat tastes way better.

00:14:28.267 --> 00:14:29.268
And these are chili cheese bites.

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:36.208
Actually, not that bad.

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:37.943
It's mostly — ooh, got a
little bit of heat to them too,

00:14:37.943 --> 00:14:39.879
the jalapeños. Yeah, these are good.

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:42.681
On to the fries. Cheesy fries.

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:46.285
Oh, man, this is really phoned in.

00:14:46.285 --> 00:14:48.754
This is really phoned
in. No effort on that.

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:52.958
Look at the bacon. It's not
crispy. It's, like, right?

00:14:54.026 --> 00:14:57.496
This is the bacon they
have at an omelet station

00:14:57.496 --> 00:14:59.999
to put in your omelet
pre-diced or whatever.

00:14:59.999 --> 00:15:01.166
But this is like, guys,

00:15:01.166 --> 00:15:03.669
it's gotta be crispy or nothing. Come on.

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:05.804
Nothing to it. It really
seems like a waste.

00:15:05.804 --> 00:15:07.806
All right, sauce-talk time.

00:15:07.806 --> 00:15:10.075
Got the sweet chili
and the smoky barbecue.

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:11.543
There's also a spicy mayo.

00:15:11.543 --> 00:15:13.712
Wasn't available at the Burger
King we went to. Oh, well.

00:15:13.712 --> 00:15:17.583
It' time for sauce talk,
"Foreign Exchange"!

00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.218
Sauce talk.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:21.487
The first one, sweet chili, boys.

00:15:21.487 --> 00:15:24.256
Sweet chili is having a moment in the UK.

00:15:25.858 --> 00:15:27.893
It's growing on me. I think
sweet chili's really nice.

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:29.828
Smoky barbecue.

00:15:29.828 --> 00:15:32.498
Oh, this is a collaboration with

00:15:32.498 --> 00:15:35.401
Bull's-Eye steak sauce, or barbecue sauce.

00:15:35.401 --> 00:15:38.671
Was a big player in the sauce
game a decade or two ago.

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:40.406
But I feel like I haven't
seen Bull's-Eye in a while.

00:15:40.406 --> 00:15:42.574
Mm, this is pretty good.

00:15:42.574 --> 00:15:43.809
Here are all the US exclusive

00:15:43.809 --> 00:15:45.477
breakfast items from Burger King.

00:15:45.477 --> 00:15:47.313
We'll start on this
end, where we will find

00:15:47.313 --> 00:15:49.048
breakfast biscuit sandwiches.

00:15:49.048 --> 00:15:50.649
Now, if you saw the McDonald's episode,

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:51.884
you'll know that I didn't really like

00:15:51.884 --> 00:15:53.752
their version of a breakfast biscuit.

00:15:53.752 --> 00:15:54.853
This is the ham, egg, and cheese.

00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:56.255
You can also get a bacon, egg, and cheese

00:15:56.255 --> 00:15:57.723
or a sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:15:57.723 --> 00:15:59.591
Now, I'm still not convinced

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:01.260
by the notion of a breakfast biscuit.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:03.595
To the UK mind, this kind
of looks like a scone.

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:06.999
I will say this one kind
of feels a bit more buttery

00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:09.635
and a bit more moist than
the McDonald's one did.

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.070
So maybe it won't be as bad.

00:16:13.739 --> 00:16:16.008
It's hard to tell if this is
actually like a scone or not.

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:18.844
This has more of a sort of bready texture

00:16:18.844 --> 00:16:20.813
than a scone does, for
the British audience.

00:16:20.813 --> 00:16:23.182
I feel like a scone tends
to be a bit more crumbly

00:16:23.182 --> 00:16:25.584
and doughy, whereas
this one is more bready.

00:16:25.584 --> 00:16:26.685
As for the flavor,

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:29.121
there is a pretty similar
flavor, I would say,

00:16:29.121 --> 00:16:31.790
in that the sort of main
taste you get is butter.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:32.825
I don't know. It's pretty good.

00:16:32.825 --> 00:16:34.693
Next up we've got the Croissan'wiches.

00:16:34.693 --> 00:16:36.428
Now, for the uninitiated, like myself,

00:16:36.428 --> 00:16:37.429
this is a breakfast sandwich,

00:16:37.429 --> 00:16:39.665
but instead of a bun or a biscuit,

00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:41.967
they use a cut-in-half croissant.

00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:43.802
These come in the form of
bacon, egg, and cheese;

00:16:43.802 --> 00:16:47.006
a sausage, egg, and cheese;
a ham, egg, and cheese;

00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:48.841
or you can get a fully loaded option,

00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:50.642
which comes with all of the above.

00:16:50.642 --> 00:16:52.745
You get the bacon, you get the ham,

00:16:52.745 --> 00:16:54.380
and you get the sausage patty.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.647
Coming from a country that is

00:16:55.647 --> 00:16:57.082
in pretty close proximity to France,

00:16:57.082 --> 00:16:58.584
I feel like I do have to speak up

00:16:58.584 --> 00:17:01.320
on behalf of my French friends out there.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.422
Because, yeah, they just
look a bit sad, really.

00:17:03.422 --> 00:17:05.657
I will say I kind of have more faith

00:17:05.657 --> 00:17:07.760
in this idea than a biscuit.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:10.696
Because at least a
croissant will be hopefully

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.798
flaky and buttery pastry

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:14.633
and not quite as dry as a biscuit will be.

00:17:14.633 --> 00:17:16.502
I will say, there are
some places in the UK

00:17:16.502 --> 00:17:19.104
that will do a ham and cheese croissant.

00:17:19.104 --> 00:17:21.273
But it's usually a full-size

00:17:21.273 --> 00:17:23.509
kind of crescent-shaped croissant,

00:17:23.509 --> 00:17:24.777
which they would just cut in half

00:17:24.777 --> 00:17:27.546
and then add the cheese, a
bit of ham, and then toast it.

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:29.148
These, I don't know.

00:17:29.148 --> 00:17:31.316
It's the fact that they've
got the small circular ones.

00:17:31.316 --> 00:17:34.153
So they've clearly been
purpose-built to be buns.

00:17:34.153 --> 00:17:35.854
I'm not really sure about that.

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:36.688
I'll try the big boy.

00:17:36.688 --> 00:17:38.857
I'll try the fully loaded Croissan'wich.

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:43.195
It's actually not the
worst delivery system,

00:17:43.195 --> 00:17:45.998
because it is quite thin,
it is quite buttery,

00:17:45.998 --> 00:17:46.965
and you do get a little bit

00:17:46.965 --> 00:17:48.834
of the flakiness that you'd expect.

00:17:48.834 --> 00:17:50.702
As much as I kind of
disagree with the concept

00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:53.072
of a Croissan'wich, if you made me choose

00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:55.007
between one of these
or a breakfast biscuit,

00:17:55.007 --> 00:17:56.008
I do think I'm choosing these,

00:17:56.008 --> 00:17:58.377
because it's closer to just a sandwich.

00:17:58.377 --> 00:17:59.244
For all the Croissan'wiches,

00:17:59.244 --> 00:18:00.879
you can also get a double-meat version.

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:02.448
So you can get double meat of the bacon,

00:18:02.448 --> 00:18:04.416
of the sausage, and of the ham.

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:06.785
I don't think you can get a
double fully loaded version,

00:18:06.785 --> 00:18:08.687
because that would just be kind of insane.

00:18:08.687 --> 00:18:10.689
Then we have two
breakfast-burrito options.

00:18:10.689 --> 00:18:13.125
We have the Egg-Normous Burrito

00:18:13.125 --> 00:18:15.761
and the breakfast burrito Jr.

00:18:15.761 --> 00:18:17.696
If this is Jr., then is this his dad?

00:18:17.696 --> 00:18:20.499
My favorite thing to do is
just invent fast-food lore.

00:18:20.499 --> 00:18:22.067
I'm not 100% sure what's
in either of these,

00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:23.035
so let's find out.

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:25.871
Oh, wow. Some sausage.

00:18:25.871 --> 00:18:28.740
[laughs] Oh, God. Oh, no.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:32.311
Oh, God. Oh, oh, there's,
like, rice in it.

00:18:32.311 --> 00:18:34.480
I mean, I've really made a mess of this.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.314
I'm sorry, guys.

00:18:35.314 --> 00:18:40.119
So, I'm seeing what looks
like half a sausage patty,

00:18:40.119 --> 00:18:43.222
some egg, and what I think is rice.

00:18:45.157 --> 00:18:46.558
Give it a quick try.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.697
That's a reasonably
palatable breakfast burrito.

00:18:51.697 --> 00:18:54.166
And then the big boy, the Egg-Normous.

00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:55.300
All right, what do we got in here?

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.102
Bacon, quite a lot of rice.

00:18:57.102 --> 00:18:58.403
I'm not seeing any sausage in this one.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:00.806
I'm pretty sure it's just
egg, bacon, and rice.

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.107
Let's give it a quick try.

00:19:03.275 --> 00:19:05.544
It's OK. So, to me, this
does taste a little bit

00:19:05.544 --> 00:19:08.213
claggy and hard to chew its way through.

00:19:08.213 --> 00:19:10.482
However, I'm told it's supposed
to come with a salsa verde,

00:19:10.482 --> 00:19:12.017
which I think they've
forgotten to give me.

00:19:12.017 --> 00:19:14.253
So, maybe if I had a salsa with it,

00:19:14.253 --> 00:19:17.089
that would ease the
digestion a little bit.

00:19:17.089 --> 00:19:19.358
Also, this is called
the Egg-Normous Burrito,

00:19:19.358 --> 00:19:20.325
but it's really not very,

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:22.494
like, this is not enormous, guys.

00:19:22.494 --> 00:19:24.296
Come on. If you're going
to call something enormous,

00:19:24.296 --> 00:19:26.498
we're in America, I
want properly enormous.

00:19:26.498 --> 00:19:29.334
And then finally we have
some French toast sticks.

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.870
What is Burger King US's beef with France?

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:34.006
They're really just going for France here.

00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:37.743
So, I don't think I've ever
had French toast before.

00:19:37.743 --> 00:19:39.545
It's not really a thing in the UK.

00:19:39.545 --> 00:19:42.948
So, in the UK, we have
eggy bread, or egg bread,

00:19:42.948 --> 00:19:44.683
which is whisked-up eggs.

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:45.918
But it's a savory thing, because we're not

00:19:45.918 --> 00:19:48.453
putting vanilla and
cinnamon and stuff in it.

00:19:48.453 --> 00:19:49.688
Harry: I will have

00:19:49.688 --> 00:19:53.091
basically just egg in bread
that I will fry in a pan

00:19:53.091 --> 00:19:55.227
and then maybe eat with some ketchup.

00:19:55.227 --> 00:19:57.663
I'm being told I have to
try this with the syrup,

00:19:57.663 --> 00:19:58.931
so let's give that a go.

00:20:00.332 --> 00:20:03.268
British person tries French
toast for the first time.

00:20:06.872 --> 00:20:07.873
I mean, it is pretty good.

00:20:07.873 --> 00:20:10.008
Joe: Yeah, of course. It's French toast.

00:20:10.008 --> 00:20:13.579
This is even more egregious than pancakes.

00:20:13.579 --> 00:20:15.547
Because this is like a churro

00:20:15.547 --> 00:20:16.748
that you then dip in syrup.

00:20:16.748 --> 00:20:18.150
Somehow that's for breakfast.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.018
Not convinced if that is
a breakfast food or not,

00:20:20.018 --> 00:20:21.019
but it's very tasty.

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:22.921
One last thing to note is
that at a US Burger King,

00:20:22.921 --> 00:20:24.723
you can actually buy
several burger options

00:20:24.723 --> 00:20:25.958
before 10:30 a.m.

00:20:25.958 --> 00:20:27.593
While they're still
serving the breakfast menu,

00:20:27.593 --> 00:20:30.696
they will also make you a
Whopper and I think a bacon king.

00:20:30.696 --> 00:20:33.198
I'm not really sure who wants
a Whopper at, like, 9 a.m.

00:20:33.198 --> 00:20:34.499
There's obviously exclusive

00:20:34.499 --> 00:20:36.168
Burger King breakfast menu items,

00:20:36.168 --> 00:20:38.370
but since the pandemic,
a lot of Burger Kings

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.072
are still working on a reduced menu.

00:20:40.072 --> 00:20:42.507
They're almost nowhere
to be found. We looked.

00:20:42.507 --> 00:20:43.709
Apparently you're only
finding them in, like,

00:20:43.709 --> 00:20:47.512
service-station locations.
So, we looked around.

00:20:47.512 --> 00:20:49.815
Couldn't find a place
that served them. Sorry.

00:20:49.815 --> 00:20:52.251
Here are some drinks that I
can't usually find in the UK.

00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:54.886
We'll start with this one,
which is Hi-C fruit punch.

00:20:54.886 --> 00:20:57.522
That's such a deeply unnatural color.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.626
Joe: American drinks, baby!

00:21:00.626 --> 00:21:02.761
High-fructose corn syrup, let's go.

00:21:02.761 --> 00:21:05.097
My British palate has not adjusted

00:21:05.097 --> 00:21:07.165
to American soft drinks yet,

00:21:07.165 --> 00:21:09.268
because this thing is aggressively sweet.

00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:10.802
This one's Dr Pepper. I can't remember

00:21:10.802 --> 00:21:13.338
if this is on the UK
Burger King menu or not.

00:21:13.338 --> 00:21:15.007
But, I mean, I like Dr Pepper in the UK.

00:21:15.007 --> 00:21:16.875
Let's see if it's the same in the US.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:19.011
OK, yeah, no, that's
actually pretty comparable.

00:21:19.011 --> 00:21:21.647
Burger King in the US also
has some milkshake options.

00:21:21.647 --> 00:21:23.682
This one is the Oreo cookie shake.

00:21:23.682 --> 00:21:25.617
This comes highly endorsed by Joe.

00:21:25.617 --> 00:21:27.552
Did you say this was your
favorite fast-food shake?

00:21:27.552 --> 00:21:29.421
Joe: I would say, yeah,
one of my favorites, yeah.

00:21:29.421 --> 00:21:30.255
One of his favorites.

00:21:30.255 --> 00:21:31.089
Joe: One of the best ones, yeah.

00:21:31.089 --> 00:21:32.524
High praise. Let's give it a try.

00:21:35.127 --> 00:21:36.928
I mean, yeah, that's delicious.

00:21:37.829 --> 00:21:41.633
That is so thick. The straw
almost isn't up to the task.

00:21:41.633 --> 00:21:44.169
Yeah, that really does taste like Oreos,

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:45.671
like the filling of the Oreo.

00:21:45.671 --> 00:21:47.272
And then if that's not
enough chocolate for you,

00:21:47.272 --> 00:21:49.908
they also have a chocolate
Oreo cookie milkshake.

00:21:49.908 --> 00:21:51.977
I mean, yeah, it's
basically the same as that

00:21:51.977 --> 00:21:53.745
but I think just with chocolate ice cream

00:21:53.745 --> 00:21:55.580
instead of vanilla ice cream as the base.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.616
Yeah, I don't think you need
to mess with the formula.

00:21:57.616 --> 00:21:59.518
Stick with the classic.
Stick with vanilla.

00:21:59.518 --> 00:22:01.553
OK, for drinks, Burger Kings in the UK

00:22:01.553 --> 00:22:03.588
also have tea and espresso,

00:22:03.588 --> 00:22:05.357
and the one we went to
didn't have hot drinks.

00:22:05.357 --> 00:22:07.559
And they also have various Capri Suns,

00:22:07.559 --> 00:22:10.595
which they did have and we did
order and they forgot them.

00:22:10.595 --> 00:22:11.930
Then we have some Burger King desserts

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.298
that we can't find in the UK.

00:22:13.298 --> 00:22:15.834
We have two options. Firstly,
chocolate chip cookies.

00:22:15.834 --> 00:22:17.903
Seems like these come in an order of two,

00:22:17.903 --> 00:22:20.672
which have cemented themselves together.

00:22:20.672 --> 00:22:23.542
They don't look brilliant. They're quite

00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:24.710
hard on the outside.

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:26.011
[cookie banging on table]

00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:28.013
Don't know if cookies are
supposed to make that noise.

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:30.749
Those are quite overbaked.

00:22:30.749 --> 00:22:33.385
Then we have a slice of
Hershey's sundae pie.

00:22:33.385 --> 00:22:34.886
I'm kind of intrigued by this.

00:22:34.886 --> 00:22:36.488
It's come pretty highly recommended to me.

00:22:36.488 --> 00:22:38.457
I like the packaging. This is quite fun.

00:22:38.457 --> 00:22:40.392
Don't bite your nails, kids.

00:22:40.392 --> 00:22:42.928
Makes it very hard to open
Hershey's sundae pies.

00:22:42.928 --> 00:22:44.596
I really don't know what
to expect from this,

00:22:44.596 --> 00:22:46.331
but I guess I'm just
going to get a scoop out

00:22:46.331 --> 00:22:47.799
and see what happens.

00:22:48.967 --> 00:22:50.635
Is it pastry on the bottom?

00:22:52.571 --> 00:22:53.839
I can't really figure out what's going on.

00:22:53.839 --> 00:22:55.941
There's, I think, like, a sort of cakey,

00:22:55.941 --> 00:22:57.743
biscuit base type thing.

00:22:57.743 --> 00:23:00.812
Yeah, that is very rich
but also very tasty.

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:05.016
If there was one menu
item that I could keep

00:23:05.016 --> 00:23:07.018
and take back with me to the UK,

00:23:07.018 --> 00:23:07.986
I don't actually know if it would be

00:23:07.986 --> 00:23:10.422
a specific menu item, or
maybe more like an ingredient.

00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:12.424
I think I would take the
bacon that you guys have

00:23:12.424 --> 00:23:14.893
at a US Burger King and
take that back to the UK.

00:23:14.893 --> 00:23:15.961
Because I feel like here it actually

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:18.830
adds something to a burger, in
terms of texture and flavor,

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:20.332
whereas in the UK it's just kind of there.

00:23:20.332 --> 00:23:21.867
Like, you don't really notice it.

00:23:21.867 --> 00:23:23.468
And if there's one menu
item that I would delete

00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:25.203
from all possible Burger King menus,

00:23:25.203 --> 00:23:26.405
I think it would be that triple Whopper.

00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:28.774
I think it just really was
everything that is wrong

00:23:28.774 --> 00:23:30.642
with American fast food in general.

00:23:30.642 --> 00:23:32.644
It's just kind of excess
for the sake of excess.

00:23:32.644 --> 00:23:33.879
You don't need that much meat.

00:23:33.879 --> 00:23:36.381
You need some kind of
lubrication in there.

00:23:36.381 --> 00:23:39.985
It's just dry, chewy,
horrible. Get rid of it.

00:23:39.985 --> 00:23:40.852
Harry: So, Joe, you've tried

00:23:40.852 --> 00:23:42.287
all of our Burger King menu items.

00:23:42.287 --> 00:23:44.156
Which one are you taking
back with you to the US?

00:23:44.156 --> 00:23:49.127
I think I like the Memphis
barbecue burgers the best,

00:23:49.127 --> 00:23:50.929
because it was like a Rodeo burger

00:23:50.929 --> 00:23:53.131
but it's bigger and it
had more stuff on it.

00:23:53.131 --> 00:23:54.866
So I think I could really get into that.

00:23:54.866 --> 00:23:57.636
Harry: Then you can knock one
thing off the UK menu forever.

00:23:57.636 --> 00:23:58.470
What's going?

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:00.672
What was it? Oh, that fake chicken.

00:24:00.672 --> 00:24:01.940
The chicken royale specifically.

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:04.543
It was the consistency of
the chicken, how it tasted.

00:24:04.543 --> 00:24:08.180
It just tasted off. It
tasted really weird.

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:12.451
Like, my body was like, "Do
not swallow. Spit out now."

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:15.687
So I feel like as a nugget
version, it would work.

00:24:15.687 --> 00:24:18.990
But as the chicken royale,

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:20.358
didn't work. It's gotta go.

